nce 2024) This profound understanding of interconnectedness is at the very heart of Johan's work and the innovative spirit of Antwerp Ecosystem Design (AEDI) or ÆĐI. Since 2024, AEDI has been applying the principles of ecosystems – namely, adaptability, resilience, and interconnectedness – to the design of complex systems far beyond the purely biological. AEDI focuses on creating integrated and sustainable frameworks, seeing projects not as isolated components but as interconnected "ecosystems" where various elements interact to achieve optimal function and impact. Their approach emphasizes:     1. Foundational AI Principles (AiF) for System Cohesion: AEDI leverages a deep understanding of AI Fundamentals (AiF) to design systems that are inherently cohesive. This means ensuring that all components, from data pathways to user interfaces, operate in a synchronized and intelligent manner, much like a well-balanced natural ecosystem.     2. Enhancing Communication within Designed Ecosystems (LLM-EH & Ai-CL): Through Large Language Model Enhancement (LLM-EH) and AI-Communication Line (Ai-CL), AEDI is developing methods to optimize communication within these complex systems. This is vital for ensuring that information flows efficiently and effectively between all "members" of their designed "ecosystems," fostering clarity and preventing breakdowns.     3. Protocol-Driven Reliability (Ai-PT): Just as natural ecosystems follow certain laws, AEDI ensures strict adherence to established protocols and procedures through AI-Protocol Training (Ai-PT). This maintains operational consistency and reliability, making their engineered ecosystems robust and dependable.     4. Intent-Driven Interactions (IO-ASPECTS-AI & AI-IR): A key focus since 2024 has been on "IO-ASPECTS-AI" and recognizing "AI-IR as an 8th Core Function" – AI-Intent Recognition. This means AEDI is designing systems that can proactively understand and respond to user intent, creating a highly efficient and intuitive